    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`stabilityai/stablelm-2-1_6b` fails on Intel XPU with a rotary-embedding dimension-mismatch error. `StablelmAttention` in `stablelm.py` only special-cases NPU dtype handling around `rotary_emb` (float32 cast-and-back) — there is no equivalent XPU branch, so q/k tensors are routed through the `sgl_kernel.rotary_embedding` fallback path in the wrong dtype on XPU.\n\n## Modifications\n\nMirror the existing `_is_npu` handling with a new `_is_xpu` check in `StablelmAttention.__init__` and `.forward`, so XPU also gets the float32 cast-and-back around `rotary_emb` that NPU already relies on.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nValidated on real Intel XPU hardware (P1 CI) running `stabilityai/stablelm-2-1_6b` against `hellaswag` via `sglang serve` + `lm_eval`:\n- Smoke run (20 examples): acc=0.35, acc_norm=0.55 — model serves and evaluates correctly with the patch applied (previously crashed with a dimension mismatch before any request completed).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Code Formatting with Pre-Commit](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-formatting-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Running Unit Tests](https://docs.sglang.ai/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#running-unit-tests-adding-to-ci) section.\n- [x] Update documentation as needed, including docstrings or example tutorials.\n\n---\nAutomated by the P1_Failure_Analysis pipeline. JIRA: SGLANGT-1710\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35973849471](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35973849471)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35973849243](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35973849243)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35973849399](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35973849399)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
